This extension adds Nioh 3 modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]Yumia and DLL Loader automatically installed.[/summary]

[b][color=#ffff00]The extension will automatically download and install the following mods:[/color][/b]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/nioh3/mods/49]DLL Plugin Loader[/url]﻿[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/nioh3/mods/90]Loose Files Loader[/url]﻿[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/nioh3/mods/84]Nioh3ModManager[/url]﻿[/*]
[/list]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Steam Demo[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]DLL Plugin Loader installs to the game folder, recognised by a "dinput8.dll" file.[/*]
[*]RDBExplorer mods with a "RDBExplorer.exe" file install to the "package" folder.[/*]
[*]Yumia fdata Tools mods with a "yumia_mod_insert_into_rdb.exe" file install to the "package" folder.[/*]
[*]Loose File Loader installs to the "plugins" folder, recognised by a "LooseFileLoader.dll" file.[/*]
[*]ModManager mods with a "Nioh3ModManager.exe" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]ModManager Loose mods with a ".g1t", ".g1m" or ".g1ts" file install to the "ModArchives" folder.[/*]
[*]Plugin mods with a ".dll" or ".asi" file install to the "plugins" folder.[/*]
[*]Package (Yumia) mods with a "package" folder and a ".fdata" or ".yumiamod.json" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Any other mod not described above installs to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]Automatically installs [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/nioh3/mods/49]DLL Plugin Loader[/url]﻿ to the game root folder.[/*]
[*]Automatically installs [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/nioh3/mods/90]Loose Files Loader[/url]﻿ to the "plugins" folder[/*]
[*]Automatically installs [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/nioh3/mods/84]Nioh3ModManger [/url]to the game root folder.[/*]
[*].g1t/.g1m Loose Files Mods are zipped and placed in the "ModArchives" folder for the ModManger ﻿﻿to install. ModManger installs them to the "mods" folder based on options selected.[/*]
[*]You will get a notification to run the ModManger on each deployment where you can select options and complete mod installation.[/*]
[*][color=#ffff00][size=2][b]The first time you launch Nioh3ModManger after deploy, you must set the "Mods Directory" to the "ModArchives" folder (in game root).[/b][/size][/color][/*]
[*]Vortex will send a notification to run the ModManager after each deployment.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Nioh 3 mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

DLL Plugin Loader:

Recognised when the archive contains a "dinput8.dll" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

RDBExplorer:

Recognised when the archive contains a "RDBExplorer.exe" file.

  Installs to: "package"

========================================================================

Yumia fdata Tools:

Recognised when the archive contains a "yumia_mod_insert_into_rdb.exe" file.

  Installs to: "package"

========================================================================

Loose File Loader:

Recognised when the archive contains a "LooseFileLoader.dll" file.

  Installs to: "plugins"

========================================================================

ModManager:

Recognised when the archive contains a "Nioh3ModManager.exe" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

ModManager Loose Mod:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".g1t", ".g1m" or ".g1ts" file.

  Installs to: "ModArchives"

========================================================================

Plugin Mod:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".dll" or ".asi" file.

  Installs to: "plugins"

========================================================================

.fdata Package (Yumia):

Recognised when the archive contains a "package" folder and a ".fdata" or ".yumiamod.json" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Fallback Installer:

The catch-all. Any archive that matched none of the installers above lands here and is copied across unchanged.

[b][color=#ffff00]NOTE: Landing in the fallback installer is a signal your archive layout needs fixing.[/color][/b]

  Requirements:
    - Reaching this installer usually means the archive was not laid out in a way Vortex recognised.
    - Vortex shows the user a notification when a mod installs through the fallback.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - If your mod lands here unintentionally, re-check the layouts above - users will see a fallback warning and may report the mod as broken.

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives that contain a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with "ModuleConfig.xml") are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead, and none of the rules above apply.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]
